                        <div class="location-template-history-footer">
                            <h3 class="heading-m">A history that gives the quarter its soul</h3>
                            <p class="text-m">From its very beginnings, the Volta Quarter has been a creator of modern urban space – in 1913, the Volta factory achieved the capacity to produce electricity, enabling the city of Tallinn to receive its first street lighting. The factory’s main products were electric motors. Today, the gold-toned 10,000,000th electric motor can be viewed in the lobby of the 47B Lofts.</p>
                            <p class="text-m">Alongside electric engines, Volta has produced a wide range of goods over the years, including perfumes, confectionery, knitwear, as well as radiators and much-loved waffle machines familiar in Estonian households. It is precisely the design of these waffle irons that has inspired the exterior architecture of Volta Residences.</p>
